--- RE-RUN 2026-10-10: browser enforcement sub-steps — RAN ---
browser: Playwright headless Chromium. Demos: fresh headers-demo.py
(SECURED=1) plus a controlled page sending the same CSP header, loopback only.
Step 3 (CSP enforcement): page reflecting an UNENCODED inline-handler payload
(<img src=x onerror="window.__fired=1">) with header
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'
loaded in the real browser: window.__fired stayed false (handler did NOT
execute); console logged "Executing inline event handler violates the
following Content Security Policy directive 'default-src ...'". The block is
browser behavior, observed — not just header presence.
Step 4 (frame refusal): cross-origin attacker page (127.0.0.1:18096) framing
the SECURED demo (127.0.0.1:18098, sends frame-ancestors 'self' and
X-Frame-Options: DENY): the subframe never committed — its URL is
chrome-error://chromewebdata/, body length 0; console logged "Framing
'http://127.0.0.1:18098/' violates the following Content Security Policy
directive: "frame-ancestors 'self'"". Refused for real.
(Correction logged, not smoothed: the first attempt framed same-origin, which
frame-ancestors 'self' correctly ALLOWS — the refusal only manifests
cross-origin, which is the actual clickjacking threat model.)
HSTS (step 6) enforcement remains browser behavior verified as sent only —
the honest boundary stated in the lesson stands.
